10
00:56:31,304 --> 00:56:37,304
Green Book is a 2018 American biographical
comedy-drama film directed by Peter Farrelly.

11
01:02:10,434 --> 01:02:16,434
Starring Viggo Mortensen and Mahershala Ali, the film is inspired by the true story of a 1962 tour of the Deep South by African-American pianist
Don Shirley and Italian-American bouncer and later actor Frank "Tony Lip" Vallelonga, who served as Shirley's driver and bodyguard.

12
01:07:49,565 --> 01:07:55,565
Written by Farrelly alongside Lip's son Nick Vallelonga and Brian Hayes Currie, the film is
based on interviews with Lip and Shirley, as well as letters Lip wrote to his wife.

13
01:13:28,695 --> 01:13:34,695
It is named after The Negro Motorist Green Book, a guide book for African-American
travelers founded by Victor Hugo Green in 1936 and published until 1966.

14
01:19:07,826 --> 01:19:13,826
Green Book had its world premiere at the Toronto International Film Festival
on September 11, 2018, where it won the People's Choice Award.

15
01:24:46,956 --> 01:24:52,956
It was then theatrically released in the United States on November 16, 2018,
by Universal Pictures, and grossed $321 million worldwide.

16
01:30:26,086 --> 01:30:32,086
The film received positive reviews from critics, with praise for the performances of Mortensen and
Ali, although it also drew some criticism for its depiction of both race and Shirley.

17
01:36:05,217 --> 01:36:11,217
Green Book received many awards and nominations.

18
01:41:44,347 --> 01:41:50,347
It won the Academy Award for Best Picture, Best Original
Screenplay, and Best Supporting Actor (for Ali).

19
01:47:23,478 --> 01:47:29,478
It also won the Producers Guild of America Award for Best Theatrical Motion Picture, the Golden Globe Award for Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy, and the
National Board of Review award for the best film of 2018, and was chosen as one of the top 10 films of the year by the American Film Institute.

20
01:53:02,608 --> 01:53:08,608
Ali also won the Golden Globe, Screen Actors Guild, and
BAFTA Awards for Best Supporting Actor.

21
01:58:41,739 --> 01:58:47,739
The film explores themes of friendship, southern usa,
based on true story, road trip, racism.

22
02:04:20,869 --> 02:04:26,869
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and thought_provoking.
